cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, its method or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "jev-laya-classification-bench: Typed-decision models versus an LLM on 12,000 federal IT solicitations"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kinge
    given-names: Bhushan
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-24
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/bhushankinge/jev-laya-classification-bench"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark of typed-decision models (the Jev API, jev-1.13.0, and its 421M-parameter open-weights
  sibling Laya) against Qwen3.5-35B-A3B on 12,000 real U.S. federal IT solicitations, graded against the
  product types a reseller actually quoted. On 741 paired rows with quote gold, Jev reaches 91.9% primary-class
  accuracy with ECE 0.049 and auto-accepts 86.5% of rows at a Wilson-bounded 95% precision; Qwen reaches 89.6%
  and Laya 78.0%, neither reaching a 95% cutoff. Fulfillment mode (distributor SKU versus OEM-configured build)
  stays at or below 71% for every model.
keywords:
  - text classification
  - typed decisions
  - calibration
  - selective prediction
  - LLM evaluation
  - federal procurement
  - benchmark
